12.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority (cols 1,3,4,6,7,10,11,12,15,18) converge on A: standard map thr-leu-azi-ton-pro-lac; azi proximal only if origin immediately upstream of azi (near ton) with polarity sending azi first, producing long gap before next markers. This matches “prolonged early azi expression.” Direction labeled clockwise on conventional map.  
Dissent: cols 13/14/8 pick B (lac origin, counterclockwise) claiming azi enters “relatively early”; cols 16/17/2/5 pick D (thr origin, counterclockwise) citing classic HfrH order O-thr-leu-azi. Both place azi later or require different polarity, contradicting “before others.”  
Key facts preserved: map order fixed; only ton-proximal + correct polarity satisfies geometry. No external data needed. Unresolved: exact clockwise/counterclockwise convention on drawn circle, but A is only option satisfying both proximity and observed kinetics. My belief remains A.}

