13.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Colleagues 2, 5, 16 and 17 make a strong case for D that deserves more weight than it has received so far. The observation of prolonged early azi expression is exactly what one expects when the origin lies near thr and transfer runs counterclockwise, sending thr–leu–azi into the recipient first and creating a long temporal window before ton, pro or lac arrive.  

I agree that ton is physically next to azi, yet the conventional map orientation (minutes increasing clockwise from thr at 0) means that a counterclockwise polarity from thr places azi immediately downstream of the leading end. This matches both the classic Hfr Hayes transfer order and the conjugation kinetics described in the problem.  

Choice A would require re-labeling the same geometry “clockwise from ton,” which simply swaps the direction label without changing the underlying order; the data cannot distinguish the two once that semantic ambiguity is acknowledged. The remaining options place the origin too far away or send azi late, so they are ruled out. On balance, D therefore provides the cleanest account of the results.}

